<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Required for the sidebar's Network card to show the Wi-Fi
	  network's name. Since macOS 14, CWInterface.ssid() returns nil
	  unless the calling process holds location authorisation, and
	  every shell-out (networksetup, system_profiler, ipconfig) is
	  redacted — there is no path to the name that avoids this.

	  Shax never reads, stores, or transmits a location. The
	  authorisation exists solely so the OS will hand over the name of
	  the network you are already connected to. Declining costs the
	  name and nothing else: the card still reports that you are on
	  Wi-Fi.
	-->
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Shax uses this only to read the name of the Wi-Fi network you are connected to, so the sidebar can show it. Your location is never read, stored, or sent anywhere.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
